cuda-oxide backend patch carried by bloomery: NVIDIA/cuda-rust pull request #1648, "perf(cute): speed up the CuTe
verifier's provenance analysis" (fixes #1647), by juliankang4. Base 9df9e7cef561 (this tree's pin), head 4bb62e04db45;
the diff below is the pull request's, unchanged, 7 files under cuda-oxide/cute-rs-preview/dialect-cute/src/verify/.

Why it is carried. dialect-cute's verify_cute_semantics runs on every module the backend lowers, and each story builds
provenance facts for every scope, even one with no CuTe operation. OrdinaryFacts::entries scans the whole fact map for
every store and block argument inside the fixed-point loops, so the time is cubic in the block count of a kernel and
bloomery-gpu does not finish. The pull request indexes the facts by carrier, skips a story whose family has no operation
in the scope, keeps at most two opaque origins per path and checks each local cell's aliases once.

tools/oxide-backend.sh applies this file to the pin's checkout (patch -p1) and builds the backend from the copy. Drop
this file when the pin holds #1648 (the dry run in tools/oxide-backend.sh then fails by name).

